WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.870 --> 00:00:05.410
Actor Craig T. Nelson has had a long career
in Hollywood, both in film and TV, but the

00:00:05.410 --> 00:00:09.891
role he's probably best remembered for is
football coach Hayden T. Fox on the '90s ABC

00:00:09.891 --> 00:00:10.990
sitcom Coach.

00:00:10.990 --> 00:00:15.150
He won an Emmy for his work on the hit series,
and went on to star on two other long-running

00:00:15.150 --> 00:00:20.090
shows: the CBS cop drama The District and
NBC's family tearjerker Parenthood.

00:00:20.090 --> 00:00:23.670
He still pops up in movies here and there,
but for the most part, Nelson isn't as much

00:00:23.670 --> 00:00:25.800
of a screen fixture as he once was.

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:27.680
Here's what he's been up to.

00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:29.090
Letting go

00:00:29.090 --> 00:00:33.079
Nelson landed the part of patriarch Zeek Braverman
on Parenthood right after he turned down a

00:00:33.079 --> 00:00:37.010
similar role on a more popular show: ABC's
Modern Family.

00:00:37.010 --> 00:00:40.480
Nelson was offered the chance to play family
patriarch Jay Pritchett— a role that went

00:00:40.480 --> 00:00:41.510
to Ed O'Neill.

00:00:41.510 --> 00:00:45.489
In an interview with Access Hollywood Live,
Nelson said he "liked the script" and "liked

00:00:45.489 --> 00:00:49.289
the people" on Modern Family, but the producers
didn't offer him the amount of money he felt

00:00:49.289 --> 00:00:50.559
he deserved.

00:00:50.559 --> 00:00:55.030
After six seasons, Parenthood left the air
in 2015 with — spoiler alert — a pretty

00:00:55.030 --> 00:00:59.690
devastating finale: Zeek dies after a long
battle with heart problems.

00:00:59.690 --> 00:01:03.309
Nelson wasn't happy about the way his character
or the show went out, telling the Hollywood

00:01:03.309 --> 00:01:04.309
Reporter,

00:01:04.309 --> 00:01:05.390
"I think the series should have gone on.

00:01:05.390 --> 00:01:07.000
I still don't know why it was pulled."

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:10.400
He added that he "never got on board" with
his character dying, although he thought the

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:13.570
death was "really dignified, nice and emotional."

00:01:13.570 --> 00:01:15.890
Failed revival

00:01:15.890 --> 00:01:20.150
In 2015, after Parenthood came to an end,
NBC attempted to bring back ABC's Coach.

00:01:20.150 --> 00:01:23.980
The network was so confident that the Coach
revival would work, in fact, it skipped the

00:01:23.980 --> 00:01:27.630
pilot phase and ordered the show straight
to series—set to star Nelson and several

00:01:27.630 --> 00:01:29.040
other original cast members.

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:32.170
"It's gonna be a risk, y'know, it's gonna
be fun.

00:01:32.170 --> 00:01:34.040
That's what's so exciting about it.

00:01:34.040 --> 00:01:35.610
Trying to make it work."

00:01:35.610 --> 00:01:40.270
The plot focused on Hayden Fox's adopted son
Tim launching a football program at a prestigious

00:01:40.270 --> 00:01:43.490
college, and enlisting his recently widowed
father to help.

00:01:43.490 --> 00:01:48.530
But in August 2015, NBC canceled the project
after only one episode was filmed in front

00:01:48.530 --> 00:01:52.810
of a studio audience, which was never released
and has yet to be leaked.

00:01:52.810 --> 00:01:54.240
Promising pilot

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:58.880
It looked like Nelson had a big TV comeback
in the works in 2017 when he was cast in the

00:01:58.880 --> 00:02:00.730
pilot for Raised by Wolves.

00:02:00.730 --> 00:02:05.490
The comedy had an impressive pedigree: Oscar-winning
screenwriter Diablo Cody wrote the pilot,

00:02:05.490 --> 00:02:10.630
based on a British series co-created by popular
English humorist Caitlin Moran, about a single

00:02:10.630 --> 00:02:12.489
mother raising five kids.

00:02:12.489 --> 00:02:16.689
This Is Us producer Greg Berlanti came on
as an executive producer, and the cast included

00:02:16.689 --> 00:02:19.370
Georgia King of HBO's Vice Principals.

00:02:19.370 --> 00:02:23.090
ABC passed on the show, and producers tried
to shop it around to cable networks… but

00:02:23.090 --> 00:02:25.599
there haven't been any takers yet.

00:02:25.599 --> 00:02:26.599
Charity work

00:02:26.600 --> 00:02:31.060
While Nelson once famously weighed not paying
income taxes to protest the "welfare state"

00:02:31.580 --> 00:02:33.160
"I've been on food stamps and welfare.

00:02:33.160 --> 00:02:33.780
Anybody help me out?

00:02:33.780 --> 00:02:34.780
No."

00:02:35.360 --> 00:02:39.060
… he's given plenty of his time to organizations
that help others get back on their feet.

00:02:39.060 --> 00:02:43.050
Nelson has worked with a drug and alcohol
rehabilitation charity called the Drug Education

00:02:43.050 --> 00:02:48.060
Council, and spoke at the organization's annual
luncheon in 2017.

00:02:48.060 --> 00:02:51.920
In 2009, he mentioned on Hannity that he supports
Dogs For Vets, a group that pairs shelter

00:02:51.920 --> 00:02:55.840
dogs with returning military personnel, as
well as a group that grants scholarships to

00:02:55.840 --> 00:02:57.660
veterans' children.

00:02:57.660 --> 00:02:59.260
Extracurriculars

00:02:59.260 --> 00:03:02.840
The guy who played a coach in All the Right
Moves and Coach doesn't stand on the sidelines

00:03:02.840 --> 00:03:05.390
in real life—instead, he's an active golfer.

00:03:05.390 --> 00:03:10.220
In 2013, he told the Golf Content Network
that he has a handicap of eight—which, as

00:03:10.220 --> 00:03:14.689
golfers know, means Nelson is pretty good,
although he says, quote, "the ability to maintain

00:03:14.689 --> 00:03:16.359
that number seems to come and go."

00:03:16.359 --> 00:03:19.989
His strengths are chipping and putting, which
he says he'll practice for up to two hours

00:03:19.989 --> 00:03:20.989
a day.

00:03:20.989 --> 00:03:23.769
He's also a regular at celebrity-studded pro-am
tournaments.

00:03:23.769 --> 00:03:25.109
Nelson also loves motorsports.

00:03:25.109 --> 00:03:30.510
In fact, in 1991, he went to auto racing school,
and soon after entered the Toyota Celebrity

00:03:30.510 --> 00:03:32.879
Long Beach Grand Prix, finishing in third
place.

00:03:32.879 --> 00:03:36.849
At that point, Nelson said he was "hooked":
He started driving in the World SportsCar

00:03:36.849 --> 00:03:41.370
series, also known as the International Motor
Sports Association, and told Motor Trend that

00:03:41.370 --> 00:03:44.359
it was tough to break into the sport and to
be taken seriously.

00:03:44.359 --> 00:03:48.400
But Nelson proved he had the right stuff,
and was voted the racing organization's "Most

00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:52.090
Improved Driver," which he quipped "was better
than winning the Emmy."

00:03:52.090 --> 00:03:53.349
A look ahead

00:03:53.349 --> 00:03:58.480
Nelson has worked steadily since Coach ended
in 1997, and it looks like he'll be busy in

00:03:58.480 --> 00:03:59.480
2018.

00:03:59.480 --> 00:04:02.859
Nelson will join an all-star cast in the comedy
Book Club, about a group of women in their

00:04:02.859 --> 00:04:07.030
sixties whose lives get a jolt of excitement
when their book club reads—and really gets

00:04:07.030 --> 00:04:08.950
into—Fifty Shades of Grey.

00:04:08.950 --> 00:04:12.760
Nelson's most famous gig—and the one that
made the most money at the box office—involved

00:04:12.760 --> 00:04:13.980
only his voice.

00:04:13.980 --> 00:04:19.559
He was Bob Parr, a.k.a. Mr. Incredible, in
Disney/Pixar's 2004 superhero movie The Incredibles

00:04:19.559 --> 00:04:23.750
— and a sequel is in the works, set to be
released in June 2018.

00:04:23.750 --> 00:04:27.630
Plot details are scant, but director Brad
Bird said that Bob has shifted gears to become

00:04:27.630 --> 00:04:31.280
a stay-at-home dad, living in a new house
"that's a cross between a dream house and

00:04:31.280 --> 00:04:32.280
a super lair."

00:04:32.280 --> 00:04:37.800
"Brad has done such a good job on the story,
and John Walker, and it's like, it's a lot

00:04:37.800 --> 00:04:38.800
of fun.

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:41.380
And, um, I think it's gonna be great."

00:04:41.640 --> 00:04:42.639
Thanks for watching!

00:04:42.639 --> 00:04:44.879
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:04:44.879 --> 00:04:46.740
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

